@startuml Configuring an Octal PSRAM memory in memory-mapped mode and perform a read/write operations
== Initialization ==
"Application" -> "XSPI" : HAL_XSPI_Init()
"XSPI" --> "Application" : HAL_OK or HAL_INVALID_PARAM
"Application" -> "System" : XSPI HW Initialization
note right: Initialize GPIO
"System" --> "Application" :

== Configuration ==
"Application" -> "XSPI" : HAL_XSPI_SetConfig()
note right: Global configuration
"XSPI" --> "Application" : HAL_OK or HAL_ERROR or HAL_INVALID_PARAM

"Application" -> "XSPI" : HAL_XSPI_SendRegularCmd()
note right: Program the OCTAL PSRAM to read/write
"XSPI" --> "Application" : HAL_OK or HAL_ERROR

"Application" -> "XSPI" : HAL_XSPI_StartMemoryMappedMode()
note right: Enter the memory mapped mode
"XSPI" --> "Application" :

== Process ==
"Application" -> "System" : Read/Write
note right: Read/Write from internal memory
"System" --> "Application" :
"Application" -> "XSPI" : HAL_XSPI_StopMemoryMappedMode()
note right: Exit the memory mapped mode
"XSPI" --> "Application" :
@enduml